  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nsin θ – cosec θ = sqrt 2 \n\n**Concept used:**\n\n(a³ – b³) = (a – b)³ + 3ab(a – b)\n\ncosec θ = (1)/(sin θ) \n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ (sin3 θ – cosec3 θ ) = (sin θ – cosec θ)³ + 3 × ( sin θ × cosec θ) × (sin θ – cosec θ)\n\n⇒ Putting the values, we get\n\n⇒ (sin3 θ – cosec3 θ ) = (sqrt 2 )³ + 3((sin θ)/(sin θ))(sqrt 2 ) \n\n⇒ (sin3 θ – cosec3 θ ) = 2sqrt2+3sqrt2=5sqrt2\n\n**Therefore, the value of sin3 θ – cosec3 θ is 5sqrt 2 .**\n\nb",
